ranked.rule:
PRE-DECLARE with date -u before any run (nn_x/w5/logs/E_catgrad_predeclared.txt).
Stage S (futility; LAST checkpoint, paired per seed vs abl_base). CONTINUE iff all of:
- (s1) pooled val Δ >= -0.0010 AND holdout Δ >= -0.0005;
- (s2) 2-ep diversity margin rho(base23, base24) - ½[rho(arm23, base24) + rho(arm24, base23)] >= +0.003 (within-feed z; base-base 0.9778; scale: no_aux +0.0054, lnorm_batch +0.0016, xdrop_pop +0.0185);
- (s3) mechanism: the within-category component's cross-seed corr falls by >= +0.002 vs base-base 0.9735.
Otherwise CLOSED.
Stage E (decision; selected ckpt, @last info). PASS iff all of:
- (d1) pooled member val >= -0.0010 AND holdout >= -0.0005 vs w5_e10_base_s951/952, no val slice (M<50, M>=50, Tue, Thu) < -2 SE, pmix >= -1 SE;
- (d2) div_readout: rho_bb - rho_x >= +0.005 on val (holdout margin > 0);
- (d3) 2-member pool >= -0.0005 on val and holdout.
On PASS: s953/954 + n2cpv3 FT + decide7 with T1 = G3 + catgrad(4) and T2 = F10 + F7x + catgrad(4). Dec-7 family-candidate iff T1 V >= +0.0005 AND H >= +0.0005 (>= +1 SE), slice and pmix vetoes, presub_gate PASS. Pick 1 changes only by the frozen rule (H >= +2 SE, V >= 0).
Information only: member corr to base (target <= 0.92), the within/between split, and the composite base-category + catgrad-within.

ranked.spec:
Code (<= 1 day, nn_x/w5/model.py + train.py, write-new + mv, flag-off identity / AST test):
- Ranker kwarg `joint_layers=0`, stored in cfg only when > 0. Build last under `extra_init(offset=...)`:
  - `self.joint = nn.ModuleList([Block(d, heads, drop, ff, sim_bias=1 if sim_bias else False, gate=attn_gate, split_kv=split_kv, attn_drop=attn_drop) for _ in range(joint_layers)])`;
  - `self.seg = nn.Embedding(3, d)`, zero-init (segment: user / history / candidate).
- forward, when joint_layers > 0 (assert arch == 'tf' and use_hist):
  - after building c (incl. retrieval and dvec) and h = h_ln(...), skip hist_enc / cross / sets;
  - X = cat([u, h, c], 1) + seg; km = cat([ones, hmask, cmask], 1), N = 1 + K + M;
  - if sim_bias: bias = zeros(B, N, N); bias[:, 1+K:, 0] = cos(c, un); bias[:, 1+K:, 1:1+K] = S; other entries 0. The existing Attn bias path scales it per head and masks the keys;
  - `for blk in self.joint: X = blk(X, km, bias=bias)`; c = X[:, 1+K:]; then the unchanged dvec + head + wide.
- train.py flag `--joint_layers N`.
- Arm `E:joint) echo "--joint_layers 4 --blocks 0 --hist_layers 0"` on E_BASE + HYG, seeds 951/952 vs w5_e10_base_s951/952.
- Optional 2-epoch futility screen first: A_BASE + the same flags, seeds 23/24, vs w5/abl base.
- Memory: the dense float mask disables flash attention, about 30-45 GB per run, so 1-2 runs per GPU under the >= 60 GB-free rule.

ranked.coverage_check:
Not in COVERAGE_MAP. Nearest rows:
- hl2 / blocks3 (capacity; 10-epoch Δρ 0.0025, null);
- typed_cross (r6 typed FAIL: a key mask inside the cross block);
- cset (candidate retrieval + cosine prior in set attention: no diversity at 10 epochs);
- F10 GRU (encoder swap only);
- r7 block forms 0/13 (norms, residuals, FFN, diff-attention inside the same topology);
- 'generative recsys HSTU / OneRec / TIGER CLOSED' (PRETRAIN_PLAN §5: closed as same-data pre-training, not as a discriminative joint ranker);
- nnx_design P4 'OneTrans grouped LN' (a parameterisation detail, never run);
- EXTERNAL_TOP1 §4 #6 'D3 model-5 clone' (joint transformer, never run). D3 also drops the cvnd inputs, filters the history and uses ListMLE, so it would inherit the pop-free deficit (-0.0025 val / -0.008 holdout). JOINT changes the topology only and keeps every input and the loss.
Rejected alternatives considered:
- Perceiver-latent multi-interest bottleneck and category-token history: same tf function class, lower Δρ prior;
- no-cross retrieval-only model: the mirror of no_retr (rate 3.8);
- sigmoid attention: diff2 showed no diversity margin.

ranked.mechanism:
The difference is the LABEL RELATION, not the inputs. On production train feeds (~95% of training weight), the production ranker has already absorbed popularity and listing age, so the click relation the base mostly learns is confounded (AUDIT_1112 §3.1 item 6):
- popularity slopes are compressed ~5x (it_hist_all_luo 0.020 vs 0.097 on val);
- seq_cv_pop and f4 listing age FLIP sign (-0.017 vs +0.095; -0.025 vs +0.142);
- f1 / f3 / f5 / feed_cat_share are 1.14-1.32x stronger;
- random-like train feeds match val within 0.85-1.15x.
The base undoes all of this through one domain token. DW3 re-weights the main listwise loss so random-like feeds carry ~17.5% of it instead of 5.2% (3.4x). Its function is therefore anchored on the unconfounded relation, and members should disagree exactly along the popularity / listing-age (cold-positive) axis. Today's measurements show this axis has the best decorrelation per unit of strength: pop-free pool margin 0.015 at -0.0025 val; pop1 at 2 epochs 0.0137 at -0.0012; about 4:1 for everything else. DW3 moves along that axis WITHOUT removing the popularity inputs; removing them is what cost pop-free its 0.008 holdout.

